---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"
import FeedItem from "../components/FeedItem.astro"
import { site } from "../data/site"
import { getPosts } from "../lib/posts"

const posts = (await getPosts()).slice(0, 5)
---

<Base>
  <section class="intro prose">
    <h1>Hi, I'm Adesh.</h1>
    <p>
      I'm a senior research engineer at <a href="https://www.delfina.com/">Delfina Care</a>, where I build AI agents to
      improve pregnancy care and the decisions made around it. Most of my work is on alignment and evaluation: the
      harnesses, LLM-as-a-judge systems, and other tooling that tell us whether an agent is actually doing what we think
      it's doing.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm optimistic about what AI can do in healthcare, especially for clinicians who are stretched thin and burnt out.
      I'm also worried about agents we can't fully oversee or that learn to mislead us, and about people, including a new
      generation of AI-native clinicians, growing complacent about checking them. In high-stakes medical decisions, AI
      could be our best friend or our worst enemy. I want to help make it the former.
    </p>
    <p>
      Previously, I did my Ph.D. at the University of Toronto in the{" "}
      <a href="https://www.neurorehab-systems.ca/">Adaptive Neurorehabilitation Systems Lab</a>, using wearable cameras
      and computer vision to support clinical decision-making in neurorehabilitation.
    </p>
    <p>Based in New York City. The best way to reach me is <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 class="section-title">Recent</h2>
    {posts.map((post) => <FeedItem post={post} />)}
    <p class="more"><a href="/posts/">All writing and updates →</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
